<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.6 percent.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.6 percent in the week to May 21 compared with the equivalent week a year ago, the Bank of England said. Last week the rise was 6.0 percent.</p>
<p>NOTES IN CIRCULATION (IN ROUNDED BILLION STG)</p>
<p>			    Latest week     pvs week     year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation   21.46		21.24	  20.33</p>
<p> Bankers' deposits	 2.31		 2.16	   1.87</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
